WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:07.460
- [Mark] All right Ke, welcome back.

00:00:07.460 --> 00:00:09.070
- [Ke] Thank you for having me back.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.130
- So it hasn't been that
long since we spoke,

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.583
it was like a month or so.

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:15.960
- [Ke] Maybe two weeks.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:16.800
- [Mark] Only two weeks?

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.990
- [Ke] Yeah
(Mark mumbles)

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:23.893
- [Mark] But how have things
been since I posted your video?

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:27.963
- Actually, they've
been kinda good and bad.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:33.710
The good part, let's start with the good

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:37.420
because the good is always
the greatest part of it all.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:42.420
So the good part about
it is I did what I said

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:43.950
I wanted to do.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:46.020
I said, I wanted to be the
parent that made it back

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:47.730
and I made it back.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:52.040
I've currently been living
in a home with my children,

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:53.280
all three of them.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.460
- [Mark] You are in Carson?

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:55.950
- Yes in Carson.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:58.170
- I was able..
- [Mark] Far from Skid Row.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:01:01.030
- Very far from skid row (laughing)

00:01:01.030 --> 00:01:05.180
I was able to set aside some
differences with family members

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:07.880
that worked things out for my better

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:10.283
to where I was able to
get back to my kids.

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:14.380
But it was a battle to get there.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:15.880
Before I got there,

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:19.440
I actually had to reach my breaking point.

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:24.440
What I mean by that is, I went
through a couple of obstacles

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:29.400
that kinda slowed me down.

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:32.040
And me trying to figure out
if I'm supposed to stay here

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:34.630
or if I'm supposed to go,

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:39.630
like this life is not meant
for you to get content

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:41.453
and stuck and stagnated.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:46.730
Well, I got stuck. I got comfortable.

00:01:46.730 --> 00:01:50.590
And I couldn't get the
wake up call that I needed

00:01:50.590 --> 00:01:53.160
so it took something a
little bit more severe

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:55.950
for me to actually wake up.

00:01:55.950 --> 00:02:00.040
The guy that I spoke about
in the first interview

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:03.940
I tried so hard to build
with this person, right?

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:07.993
So this man brutally attacked me.

00:02:09.010 --> 00:02:14.010
When I say from six and
Sanford, this man attacked me

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:23.023
where I was barely able
to escape with my life.

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:27.530
I was so in fear, everybody in the hotel

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:30.580
or whatever you wanna call it, the SRO.

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:33.253
I cried for help, no one came for help.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:37.310
These people actually sat by
and watched this man abuse me

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:39.130
and could not give a lending hand

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:40.900
because they are so in fear

00:02:40.900 --> 00:02:42.970
or they feel like it's not their business.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:46.113
Things like this are not right.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:50.430
This man stopped and
forced me to walk with him

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:53.430
to the store on Wall.

00:02:53.430 --> 00:02:54.520
Is that Wall?

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.630
No, San Pedro in Seventh Street

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:58.570
which is the Green Apple, right?

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:03.030
Inside this store this man
continued to brutally attack me.

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.160
And all the people in the store had to say

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.050
was can you please leave the store?

00:03:07.050 --> 00:03:08.780
I'm begging this woman.

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:11.920
I had a seizure the other
day ma'am can you help me?

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:15.540
I'm pregnant, like this man
is sucking me in my hand,

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:20.540
he's doing all this stuff
to me and no one cared.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:24.330
I felt so bad cause like is
this really what the world

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:25.163
has come to?

00:03:26.274 --> 00:03:28.010
When we see people going through stuff

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:31.960
and we cannot stop just
to lend a helping hand.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:34.520
So immediately I called my mother-in-law

00:03:35.425 --> 00:03:37.380
who is my children's grandmother.

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:38.770
And I explained the story to her

00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:40.870
and she asked me, she said, are you ready?

00:03:41.850 --> 00:03:43.303
Are you truly ready?

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:46.980
And at that moment I knew what she meant.

00:03:47.950 --> 00:03:48.923
Yes, I'm ready.

00:03:50.010 --> 00:03:51.640
Yes, I'm ready.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:53.410
I will leave all of this stuff behind

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:56.510
just to have that moment with my children.

00:03:56.510 --> 00:03:59.380
Barely escaping downtown with my life,

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:01.890
I was just so excited
to get back to my kids

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:04.170
that I didn't care that I
didn't have a pot to piss in,

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:07.620
I didn't have a dollar
to spend on anything.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:10.180
Just being reunited with my babies

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:13.473
made everything worth my while.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.360
I was so excited.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:20.790
And I really pray that whatever it is

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:23.743
that this guy is going
through, he gets through it.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:28.996
Like, no one in this world
should be left alone.

00:04:28.996 --> 00:04:31.520
- [Mark] And what are you
gonna about with the baby?

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:34.970
- I'm gonna continue to go
through with my pregnancy.

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:36.100
I'm gonna take care of my child

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:38.670
just like I take care of the
rest of my other children

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:42.263
and we're gonna grow from
it and that's all we can do.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.140
I've reached my downfall.

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:47.120
I hit my rock bottom.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:48.010
I got my wake up.

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.990
Unfortunately, a lot of
people are not blessed

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:51.630
to get that wake up call

00:04:51.630 --> 00:04:53.670
to where they're like,
okay well I really need

00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:57.740
to make this change now
before something bad happens.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:58.903
I was able to.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:03.283
And with no hesitation, I took it and ran.

00:05:04.910 --> 00:05:07.550
- [Mark] Do you miss anything
about the past lifestyle

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:08.520
that you had?

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:10.270
I assume you've given up drugs too?

00:05:11.440 --> 00:05:14.020
- No, I don't miss getting high.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:15.880
The only thing I would say that I miss

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:18.280
is some of the good people
that I met down here.

00:05:19.150 --> 00:05:19.983
That's it.

00:05:19.983 --> 00:05:21.511
- [Mark] Are you talking
about here or Figueroa Street?

00:05:21.511 --> 00:05:22.740
- Here, Skid Row.

00:05:22.740 --> 00:05:23.770
- [Mark] Okay, cause you
were only in Skid Row

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:24.650
for a short time.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:27.230
- Yeah, but I met some
beautiful people here.

00:05:27.230 --> 00:05:28.380
- [Mark] Yeah there're
some cool people here.

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:32.520
- Like some that gave me
food when I didn't have it,

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:37.520
clothes, a place to stay, all
of that, like I felt good.

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:41.370
So if I'm gonna miss anything

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:44.433
it's just gonna be the
people that I've met.

00:05:44.433 --> 00:05:45.980
- [Mark] And what about working Figueroa?

00:05:45.980 --> 00:05:48.870
- I'm not gonna miss
any of that (chuckling).

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:50.070
Fig no.

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:53.080
But it is something that I
do want people to understand

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:56.990
about this because they
look at these girls,

00:05:56.990 --> 00:05:59.470
and they say, "well, if she
can make all this money"...

00:05:59.470 --> 00:06:00.303
- [Mark] You're talking
about Figueroa now?

00:06:00.303 --> 00:06:01.157
- [Ke] Yes.

00:06:01.157 --> 00:06:01.990
- [Mark] Which is very
different from the Skid Row.

00:06:01.990 --> 00:06:03.467
- [Ke] Yes. Very different
from Skid Row, right?

00:06:03.467 --> 00:06:04.670
(Mark mumbles)

00:06:04.670 --> 00:06:08.670
So they say, "they make
all this money" right?

00:06:08.670 --> 00:06:13.670
But if we're living realistically, $500

00:06:13.690 --> 00:06:18.690
it's $80 a night to stay in a
low budget motel, $80 a night.

00:06:23.070 --> 00:06:26.740
So if you do the math and
times that times seven

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:29.043
that $500 that they make daily,

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:33.000
it's not really help.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:35.120
And then let's face it
nine times out of 10

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:38.650
half the women out here
that are working the streets

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:40.820
are working with a man.

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:43.470
And this man don't give a
crap about where you sleep

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:45.130
or where you stay,

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:47.800
he just care about all the
money that you bring in.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:49.610
So that he can look a certain type of way

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:51.070
or he can like....

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:52.920
- [Mark] And do you get
robbed some of the time?

00:06:52.920 --> 00:06:56.462
- Yeah, like and half the girls get robbed

00:06:56.462 --> 00:06:58.280
and it doesn't actually have to mean

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:01.693
that they're robbing you for your money.

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:05.210
They may be robbing you for the product

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:07.660
and you never see the money.

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:10.481
So it's like it's backstories to it,

00:07:10.481 --> 00:07:14.340
and I wish instead of people judging

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:17.010
they would actually take the
time to actually figure out

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:20.110
who these women are and
why they do what they do

00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:23.280
or what led them to do these things.

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:26.210
Because nine times out
of 10, at 18 years old

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:27.950
you have this savvy man

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:31.060
in your ear that's just giving
you all these sweet dreams

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:34.380
as a child, cause that's
what you are at the age of 18

00:07:34.380 --> 00:07:35.653
you don't know anything.

00:07:37.530 --> 00:07:39.940
This man tells you something
that sounds so good,

00:07:39.940 --> 00:07:43.060
and yet he has on his
fancy clothes, his jewelry,

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.878
oh you're gonna be naive enough to believe

00:07:45.878 --> 00:07:47.833
everything he's gonna tell you.

00:07:49.090 --> 00:07:50.790
You don't know anything.

00:07:50.790 --> 00:07:54.780
They start off as babies
and get brainwashed

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:59.580
into thinking that this
lifestyle is okay and it's not.

00:07:59.580 --> 00:08:02.010
And I really pray that somebody's daughter

00:08:02.010 --> 00:08:07.000
or someone's son has
mercy upon human nature

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:10.240
and decide that we gotta end it.

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:11.283
We have to end it.

00:08:13.530 --> 00:08:18.530
It's more things into life
where we can fund our....

00:08:22.505 --> 00:08:27.430
We can fund our habits,
whether it's clothes, jewelry,

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:29.620
you know, drugs, stuff like that.

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:33.130
There's other ways to
support these habits.

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:35.500
And we don't know these things

00:08:35.500 --> 00:08:39.540
because we're only given
so much to work with.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:44.510
And it's sad, but I'm glad
that my story ended up

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:50.400
shedding light because
it's a whole backside of it

00:08:53.900 --> 00:08:57.280
that a lot people really don't understand.

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:00.000
Oh she pays this man, or she does this.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:03.110
Some women actually get
turned out with a man

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:06.410
where they don't have
the ability to leave.

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:08.810
This man has burned
bridges with your family,

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:11.300
he has taken you out of state

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:14.083
or whatever the coincidence may be.

00:09:15.730 --> 00:09:18.793
It's not always that the
woman wants to do this.

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:21.207
It's deeper than that.

00:09:21.207 --> 00:09:24.140
And a lot of people,
like I said categorize us

00:09:25.075 --> 00:09:28.890
as all these working women
instead of figuring out

00:09:30.570 --> 00:09:32.610
what can I do to help you?

00:09:32.610 --> 00:09:36.593
What is it that has you
so tied to this lifestyle?

00:09:38.620 --> 00:09:42.010
I've seen several women die behind this.

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:44.700
Literally blocks away from where...

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:48.083
Not even blocks a block away
from where I used to stand.

00:09:49.120 --> 00:09:51.510
Mass murderers like...

00:09:51.510 --> 00:09:53.440
Stuff like this is real

00:09:53.440 --> 00:09:55.090
and you wouldn't want your
daughter to go through it

00:09:55.090 --> 00:09:56.350
so why would you sit back

00:09:56.350 --> 00:09:59.670
and watch another one's
daughter go through it?

00:09:59.670 --> 00:10:04.350
Or someone's sister, mother, it's painful.

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:06.830
And I really hope that one day

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:11.830
we all wake up and stop living
in so much hate and greed

00:10:14.250 --> 00:10:16.050
cause that's what the world has come to.

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:19.720
It's so much evil, so
much hate, so much greed.

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:21.020
And it doesn't have to be.

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:23.980
- [Mark] You remind me
very much of another girl

00:10:23.980 --> 00:10:25.380
that I interviewed on my channel Kelly,

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:30.380
who chose to walk away from
this lucrative lifestyle.

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:32.830
ended up on Skid Row
temporarily just like you did

00:10:32.830 --> 00:10:34.213
just for a short time.

00:10:34.213 --> 00:10:35.046
- Yeah.

00:10:35.046 --> 00:10:35.879
- [Mark] Didn't like it.

00:10:35.879 --> 00:10:37.830
And you know, I helped
her with that situation

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:39.990
and my viewers did a donation campaign

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.540
and we helped her tremendously.

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:46.580
But it's a very remarkable
woman who has the strength

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:51.540
and the mental strength to
walk away from that life

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:54.760
and build another life from the ground up.

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:56.910
I mean, she got a nice
boost from that campaign,

00:10:56.910 --> 00:10:58.300
but you're doing it on your own.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:01.560
- Yes. And then see the
crazy thing about it is,

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:03.580
some of us are not fortunate enough

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:06.090
to have that mind frame.

00:11:06.090 --> 00:11:07.110
- [Mark] Yeah. It takes a lot of strength.

00:11:07.110 --> 00:11:09.450
- Exactly. I don't know.

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:12.640
I was raised off, it takes a village

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:14.123
to raise a child, right?

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:18.673
Right now it's like, where's the village?

00:11:21.020 --> 00:11:25.000
It's like, we'd rather see
somebody go through something

00:11:26.170 --> 00:11:29.430
that we've been through
and watch them fall

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:32.620
versus give them the lesson that we took

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:36.730
from the situation that we went through,

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:38.323
to help them from falling.

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:41.710
It's like, it's sad.

00:11:41.710 --> 00:11:42.543
It's really sad.

00:11:42.543 --> 00:11:43.970
Oh, well that's not my family member

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:46.310
or, oh that has nothing to do with me.

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:48.610
Oh, it's not my business.

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:50.960
What life have we become to?

00:11:50.960 --> 00:11:53.160
To where the village
is not helping anymore.

00:11:54.960 --> 00:11:58.270
It's sad, but I'm glad
because I still have a village

00:11:58.270 --> 00:11:59.580
to help me raise my children.

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:02.060
- [Mark] Yeah, so you're
living with who now?

00:12:02.060 --> 00:12:02.893
You're living with your mom?

00:12:02.893 --> 00:12:04.440
- I'm living with my mother-in-law.

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:05.273
- [Mark] That's great.

00:12:05.273 --> 00:12:10.273
- Yes. She opened her doors to
me to come and regain a part

00:12:10.650 --> 00:12:12.720
of life that I was missing.

00:12:12.720 --> 00:12:13.560
Which was my children

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:14.830
- [Mark] And you're
doing all right things?

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:15.756
- Yes.

00:12:15.756 --> 00:12:16.589
- [Mark] There's no reason to kick you out

00:12:16.589 --> 00:12:18.240
cause you're not working the streets

00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:19.073
you're not doing drugs now.

00:12:19.073 --> 00:12:21.002
- No, I left everything.

00:12:21.002 --> 00:12:21.835
- [Mark] It's beautiful.

00:12:21.835 --> 00:12:23.430
- Just for that moment to be with my kids.

00:12:23.430 --> 00:12:25.350
To wake up with my kids in the morning

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:27.510
or to hear them playing around.

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:29.050
I left it all.

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:29.990
- [Mark] I hope you stay in this direction

00:12:29.990 --> 00:12:31.030
and keep going darling.

00:12:31.030 --> 00:12:31.863
- I do.

00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:33.730
Plan to.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.240
- [Mark] That's great.

00:12:35.240 --> 00:12:37.999
- And I appreciate you
allowing me to share my story.

00:12:37.999 --> 00:12:41.233
- [Mark] Did being able
to unload all the stuff

00:12:41.233 --> 00:12:43.140
from the last talk help you?

00:12:43.140 --> 00:12:44.810
- Yes, it did.

00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:45.702
It really did.

00:12:45.702 --> 00:12:46.535
- [Mark] I'm sure it
helped some of the viewers.

00:12:46.535 --> 00:12:47.885
- It gave me an eye opener.

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:52.190
And like I said, I've been down here

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:56.403
since I've been stagnated down here.

00:12:57.690 --> 00:13:01.720
Or let me say since I was,
because I'm no longer here

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:06.720
since I was stagnated here, I
was on a spiritual awakening.

00:13:08.860 --> 00:13:13.580
So a lot of things that
I was sheltered from

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:15.180
I was allowed to see.

00:13:15.180 --> 00:13:17.810
And I feel like he gave me a second chance

00:13:19.070 --> 00:13:23.980
and I'm gonna do any
and everything possible

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:26.660
to make sure that I don't end up back here

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:27.878
or on Figueroa.

00:13:27.878 --> 00:13:30.200
- [Mark] Yeah. They're both terrible.

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:31.670
- They're both terrible places.

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:32.503
- [Mark] In different ways but...

00:13:32.503 --> 00:13:34.330
- In very different ways,

00:13:34.330 --> 00:13:39.330
but the outcome and the ending
have very much similarities.

00:13:41.363 --> 00:13:42.650
- [Mark] Yeah, they're very destructive.

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:44.280
- Yeah.
- [Mark] Lifestyles.

00:13:44.280 --> 00:13:46.440
- You get nothing out of it.

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:48.403
Fast money does not last long.

00:13:50.220 --> 00:13:51.053
At all.

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:56.470
I did touch thousands, maybe even millions

00:13:56.470 --> 00:13:58.740
I just sat in a hundred
thousand dollars cars

00:13:58.740 --> 00:14:00.920
like I did been with people

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:03.620
where we didn't establish stuff.

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:05.630
It doesn't last long

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:09.750
- For a young woman to have
the mindset to walk away

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:11.990
from the temptation of all that.

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:15.390
Is what makes Kelly's and
your stories so remarkable.

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:19.460
Maybe people don't realize
how what you guys have done

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:23.087
is so unusual.

00:14:23.087 --> 00:14:26.363
- It really is because
I mean, let's be honest.

00:14:27.460 --> 00:14:28.890
Once you get bit by the hustle bug

00:14:28.890 --> 00:14:30.220
it's kind of hard to walk away.

00:14:30.220 --> 00:14:31.470
- [Mark] Yeah, it's like a drug, right?

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:32.980
- It is like an addiction,

00:14:32.980 --> 00:14:34.410
cause it's like you always know you can go

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:36.210
and get some money fast.

00:14:36.210 --> 00:14:37.043
- [Mark] Quick easy money.

00:14:37.043 --> 00:14:40.930
